## System Hierarchy

**Decided:**
1. Bots are composed of parts. The main core is the battery, called the **JSY** ("chassis"), with randomized attachment points (e.g. head joint, 2 arm joints, 2 leg joints). Connection points only accept their matching part type. A part may have subparts, and subparts should have puzzles (not all puzzles are subparts). Each part has a volume, and each puzzle takes up volume.
2. Tools affect all puzzles; each action needs a specific tool. Two types: handheld (Hammer, Screwdriver, Feather Duster, Grinder) and large (Antenna Receiver).

**Still to decide:**
- [ ] Full randomization rules for JSY attachment points — how many head/arm/leg variants exist?
- [ ] Are more large tools needed beyond the Antenna Receiver?
- [ ] How do tools get unlocked or upgraded over time?

